    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "i mean, that sounds good in theory, but what about when a country's survival depends on it? like if a nation needs to ban certain imports to save a vital local industry from being wiped out by cheap foreign goods, but the WTO says it's illegal. shouldn't a government's first priority be its own people and economy rather than following rules made by a global committee?",
